🗓️ WEEK 10 — REAL PRODUCTS, TESTING AND FINAL FIXES

Date: Monday, 12 October 2026

🎯 Objective

The objective of Week 10 was to add real products using their printed barcodes, test the whole system end to end, and fix the remaining problems.

🛠️ Work Completed
Added the products we had actually bought, using the barcodes printed on their tags:
Puma × RCB polo — Rs. 2,999
Mufti checked shirt — Rs. 2,399
Jean Paul Gaultier parfum
Wrote 17 automated API tests in 7 groups:
pricing
database
auth
catalog and cart
Razorpay checkout
cash desk
simulated gateway
Ran a load test with 90 customers × 3 scans, 90 cash bills and 50 collections.
Tested the full flow in the browser and on a phone.
Prepared the report, UML diagrams and the presentation.

⚠️ Error / Problem Faced

The bill for the polo came to Rs. 3,538.82, more than the Rs. 2,999 printed on the tag. The MRP already includes GST, and our engine was adding 18% on top again.

The load test failed with "out of stock" because a test product had only 10 units.

On small phones, buttons were cut off and the cash amount box ran off the screen.

On college Wi-Fi, the phone could not reach the laptop.

✅ Resolution
Added MRP-inclusive pricing: for tagged items the line total is exactly the MRP, and the taxable value is MRP ÷ 1.18 = Rs. 2,541.53 with GST of Rs. 457.47.
Added the new mrp column to the existing database with a migration, without losing data.
Used high-stock products in the load test.
Fixed the layout and checked it at 375 px phone width.
Used the phone's hotspot so the phone and laptop are on the same network.
Result: 17/17 tests pass, all 3 real tags scan, and bills match the printed MRP exactly.

🖼️ Project Picture

Unified bag with the real Puma polo, Mufti shirt and JPG parfum, priced exactly at their printed MRP.

💡 Learning

We learned that real-world data (tax-inclusive MRP) can break assumptions made with test data.

We also learned the value of automated tests: every fix was checked against all 17 tests.

📐 UML CLASS DIAGRAM — COMPLETE DOMAIN MODEL
classDiagram

class Customer {
    -id
    -phone
    +login(phone)
}

class ShoppingSession {
    -sessionId
    -status
    +addItem(barcode, qty)
    +updateQuantity(itemId, qty)
    +removeItem(itemId)
    +cartView()
}

class CartLine {
    -productId
    -quantity
}

class Product {
    -barcode
    -name
    -cost
    -mrp
    -gst
    -stock
    +findByCode(code)
    +adjustStock(delta)
}

class Transaction {
    -invoiceNumber
    -grandTotal
    -paymentMethod
    -paymentStatus
    +receipt()
}

class CashShift {
    -openingCash
    -countedCash
    +collectCash(bill, amount)
    +summary()
    +close(counted)
}

class Cashier {
    -email
    -passwordHash
    +login(email, password)
}

class PricingEngine {
    +buildBill(lines)
}

class PaymentGateway {
    +createOrder(amount)
    +verifySignature()
}

Customer "1" --> "*" ShoppingSession : owns
ShoppingSession "1" *-- "*" CartLine : contains
CartLine "*" --> "1" Product : refers to
ShoppingSession "1" --> "0..1" Transaction : checks out as
Customer "1" --> "*" Transaction : pays
CashShift "0..1" --> "*" Transaction : collects
Cashier "1" --> "*" CashShift : opens
Transaction ..> PricingEngine : use
Transaction ..> PaymentGateway : use
